# state and toast patterns

- keep form state local with `useState` and `useEffect` like `components/tasks/case-modal.tsx`, `components/clients/client-modal.tsx`, `components/team/team-member-modal.tsx`, and `components/calendar/event-modal.tsx`.
- use `useToast()` from `hooks/use-toast.ts` for destructive and success feedback; use `alert()` only when matching existing settings/logout flows.
- prefer explicit handlers for `onSave`, `onClose`, and `onApply` props instead of hidden side effects.
- when reading or writing shared counts, use `lib/shared-data.ts` helpers instead of duplicating arrays.
